  "mathematical_boundary": "For fixed K>3 and arbitrarily small positive epsilon, Dprime(0)=4 epsilon(K/3-1)+o(epsilon)>0. Explicit positive short paths realize the exact initial velocities; any smooth flows with these data have the same derivative. Individual convex entropy derivatives remain nonpositive. No actual full-time path-as-flow assertion, existence theorem, novelty or original-problem closure.",
