    "proof_obligations": [
      "Declare the changed ambient space as E squared with normalized real and imaginary periods.",
      "Use the book dd^c normalization to compute dd^c cosine as minus pi cosine times eta.",
      "Normalize kappa squared mass to two and the flat probability mu to one.",
      "Use the real-torus degree-two Haar-preserving map for the two exact averages.",
      "Compute both one-variable absolute-cosine moments and the weighted double-angle moment.",
      "Normalize the fixed target exp(KP) by its finite strictly positive partition function.",
      "Keep that target fixed as epsilon tends to zero and use the same target for both paths.",
      "Verify global initial metric positivity for epsilon between zero and inverse pi.",
      "Construct actual short smooth positive paths by openness on the compact surface.",
      "Check both path velocities equal the logarithmic Monge–Ampère velocities at zero.",
      "Use closed-background mass invariance for every small-time path probability.",
      "Define pairwise total variation with the probability factor one-half.",
      "Check the full complex Hessian matrix, including off-diagonal target derivatives.",
      "Differentiate the determinant at the diagonal initial metric and at the identity.",
      "Cancel the common target term correctly while retaining the cofactor-difference forcing.",
      "Derive the uniform first-order epsilon density-velocity expansion.",
      "Compute the exact initial density difference and its cosine coefficient.",
      "Use at most two zeros per real fiber and Fubini for a null initial zero set.",
      "Justify differentiation of the absolute-value integral by a uniform smooth derivative bound.",
      "Establish almost-everywhere convergence of the sign and uniform domination in epsilon.",
      "Use both exact averages to obtain the coefficient4(K/3-1), with positive sign for K>3.",
      "Transfer the initial derivative to any smooth flows with the same initial data without an existence claim.",
      "Apply the local entropy calculation only at zero for arbitrary initial potentials, with closed forms and positive densities.",
      "Keep the pairwise growth distinct from the individual entropy law and from a novelty or original-catalogue claim."
    ],
